#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# difference_quotient

#% text
# `difference_quotient(f, [x, h])` gives the difference quotient `(f(x + h) - f(x))/h`.

#% text
# `difference_quotient(f, [x, k, h])` gives the k-th forward difference quotient; `difference_quotient(f, spec1, spec2, ...)` applies the specifications in turn.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The k-th quotient is the sum of `(-1)^(k - j) binomial(k, j) f(x + j h)` over j = 0, ..., k, divided by h^k and cancelled.

#% item
# A list of functions is mapped element-wise. The limit h -> 0 is the derivative.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
difference_quotient(x^3, [x, h])
#% output
#= 3*x^2 + 3*h*x + h^2

#% cell
difference_quotient(f(x), [x, 2, h])
#% output
#= (f(x) + f(x + 2*h) - 2*f(h + x))/h^2

#% cell
difference_quotient(f(x, y), [x, r], [y, s])
#% output
#= (f(x, y) + f(r + x, s + y) - f(x, s + y) - f(r + x, y))/(r*s)

#% cell
limit(difference_quotient(x*sin(x), [x, h]), h -> 0)
#% output
#= x*cos(x) + sin(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `d`, `difference_delta`, `limit`
